          <p class="eyebrow mb-3">Overview</p>
          <h2 class="section-title">Security from the silicon up</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="prose-content">
          <p>Software-based security runs on top of an operating system that can be compromised, circumvented, or quietly subverted. If the trust foundation is weak, every layer built above it inherits that weakness. Hardware security addresses this by anchoring trust in silicon — a TPM 2.0 chip whose keys are generated and stored in hardware, never exposed to the host OS, and whose integrity can be measured and verified at every boot stage.</p>
          <p>MEAICON's hardware security practice spans the full device lifecycle: controlled provisioning at manufacture, secure and measured boot enforcement, anti-tamper chassis monitoring, MPC-based key management for complex architectures, and secure de-provisioning at end of mission. No unit is ever left in an unknown state — chain-of-trust control is maintained from power-on through decommissioning.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

